#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e984114-5250-5e93-9511-48bac12cfb9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302847} {:answer/id #uuid "536277d2-5b8a-503d-a547-8e1ffa1619d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302973} {:answer/id #uuid "6701a2fc-b43c-561e-81c5-9a434d500329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303079} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f94bea-ca31-58fa-8503-9c6a88e5056d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303652} {:answer/id #uuid "de489d4e-47c1-57c5-b9c1-2c901e23f182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303850}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303079} :answer-field/id #uuid "30b0d329-2c9a-520a-b86a-e2e9f3f6e22f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2afa676a-abb9-5d12-aece-9211e3985b3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332613" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(3,-1)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(3,-1)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =-x+4y \\\\  & =-3+4(-1) \\\\  & =-3-4 \\\\  & =-7 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =2x+2y \\\\  & =2(3)+2(-1) \\\\  & =6-2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061b66b7-e424-5920-84cd-972890089764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302495} {:answer/id #uuid "14dc05d9-6bdd-531d-bb9f-c08a73685dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302593} {:answer/id #uuid "17ad218c-e065-5127-ba3d-cfb28ba5e91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302611} {:answer/id #uuid "a69a12a0-c505-58a3-8629-8983ca3756a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303479} {:answer/id #uuid "cd98bf2d-4245-51ce-b50e-9121e66c9f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303724}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302611} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7a495a-9b8e-544a-9e94-115a4f814bdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7ff3e0a8-326c-5726-b35a-ede39fe9f714" :question/math-academy-id "q-332614" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(0,-2)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(0,-2)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =3x-2y \\\\  & =3(0)-2(-2) \\\\  & =0+4 \\\\  & =4 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =-4x+y \\\\  & =-4(0)+(-2) \\\\  & =0-2 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "181194f5-a879-5ec2-b6c0-3af3afa6256b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302614} {:answer/id #uuid "33d8110f-c31f-5b1c-b20f-c770fe1448fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}32 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302778} {:answer/id #uuid "47b1613a-2a1c-562a-94fa-fccedeb957fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302907} {:answer/id #uuid "58e497ef-9f0b-54d2-8b77-9b4cf42e46f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 32\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302997} {:answer/id #uuid "81e67c02-d101-5e4b-8988-f95ec9dcd921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303269}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302778} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb97b647-4a7f-5a3e-b54d-1212e5f5655a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "16aaff9d-1094-5d86-8806-bdb9ead1fd45" :question/math-academy-id "q-332618" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(t)={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & ={e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+8\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2(12)+1(8) \\\\ 0(12)+3(8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}24+8 \\\\ 0+24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}32 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305074 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e168f1-354e-55c1-af8c-5a3d318e832d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302576} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7e0a79-2503-5319-9234-f0aacc72fa84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302854} {:answer/id #uuid "5e4da5d0-d6f4-5b15-a70b-428b3228e899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303030} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4bedbd-60fc-58b6-b7f8-72de905057fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303731} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2ff532-09b5-5405-83d4-e7aa3ebd453f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304053}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302576} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6127b8f-72b2-56bf-9f7c-bfaf6f77aec3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c44dc777-c533-5984-b45f-de5fb3637699" :question/math-academy-id "q-332627" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(t)={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =9\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1(10)+1(8) \\\\ 1(10)+1(8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305075 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c9f4c5-b642-5b52-b3fe-3d871abe9f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302501} {:answer/id #uuid "101d85fd-fd3b-5ad9-a521-1ea596e24363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302561} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c9d325-1250-57a6-8ee5-15ffa53be04e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303636} {:answer/id #uuid "eaff7287-f9e0-5c51-9edc-fdf858fd3182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303923}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303636} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b303948-b2b9-5382-baff-acedf20989c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304282} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef2ad08-b248-56aa-909d-36ecaff6e22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302651} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6cfa34-cba3-5612-b07d-c81d2e4e2766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303019} {:answer/id #uuid "abfe8c24-f451-59b7-acc8-83dfc098142f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303515} {:answer/id #uuid "c7da8eaf-94e8-5082-83d0-abbe6d38c21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303680}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303019} :answer-field/id #uuid "db79ad21-96b0-553c-aa3e-2d3f7dae8ca8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3c782024-64b0-58c7-9205-ffc4beaa0f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-332634" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-2x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-2x+4y=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx-y=0\\,⇒\\,y=x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/19/19c33a634af36765142e2f4b85df1b9209d3f1abf105a131b629b3249bd91c2c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d4cf49d-97f1-5b7e-ba9c-f3eb7d0e2cb2" :answe