l equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-4x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=4x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n2x+2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/1c/1c701d81ab131757758e19c3c1d9813f1e8cda3ff069843c9105dd125d1caf97.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abda45f-8558-556e-a1bb-b0a4e3466980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302527} {:answer/id #uuid "40bcf997-cdee-5695-89c8-c3cbbde37206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302864} {:answer/id #uuid "69e062fa-4806-5566-8857-76d82ed482e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303101} {:answer/id #uuid "722996f1-89f8-55ce-bb41-fc3c791182b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303150} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9fc0f3-647a-5b58-97fd-78a8d8eba4c0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304445} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c8ca152-f66b-5377-84bc-5047bc55d7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303229} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5968e7-b8d3-5e05-9429-7d9180037195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303523} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e0b8ed-a8d3-5d1f-86eb-f984690bcf0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303807} {:answer/id #uuid "fe412655-3829-58d0-bf25-07ceceb3544e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304054}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303229} :answer-field/id #uuid "b132ecb5-d8a8-5a49-9284-d88bdf5ed058" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5714cb19-05a6-5cf5-86c3-beaae7a045c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-332647" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n2x+4y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/59/59a731b27e2333fef2bfa48e9e61a7075548ddd74782c1fadf1dd98f68ef2a7e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a6a6542-883b-513d-8497-d61ff5a5d4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3x" :db/id #edb/re